From: Donnie Guedry <dguedry@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:20:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat: collect security key PINs via
 'collect-webauthn-pin' session event
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chromium's FIDO layer asks its embedder to collect a PIN through
FidoRequestHandlerBase::Observer::SupportsPIN()/CollectPIN(). Electron's
authenticator request delegate left those at the content-layer defaults
(no PIN support), so on platforms without a system WebAuthn UI — notably
Linux — a security key that requires user verification could never
complete a request: there was nowhere to ask for the PIN.

Implement the PIN observer hooks and bridge them to a new session event,
'collect-webauthn-pin', following the same pattern as
'select-webauthn-account':

- SupportsPIN() reports true only while a listener is registered for the
  event, so PIN collection is strictly opt-in and existing apps keep
  their current behavior (e.g. userVerification 'preferred' requests
  continue to complete without UV rather than being routed into a PIN
  exchange nothing can service).
- CollectPIN() emits the event with the relying party id, the reason
  ('challenge' | 'set' | 'change'), the error from a failed previous
  attempt, the authenticator's minimum PIN length, and the remaining
  attempts before hard lock. The listener answers through a callback;
  calling it with no arguments cancels the request.
- Entries are validated locally with device::pin::ValidatePIN before
  being sent to the authenticator, re-emitting the event with 'error'
  set instead of consuming one of the limited retry attempts on a PIN
  that cannot possibly be accepted — mirroring Chrome's PIN dialog.
- StartBioEnrollment() dismisses inline biometric enrollment
  immediately (the equivalent of Chrome's "skip" button) so that
  makeCredential on a biometric-capable but unenrolled key proceeds
  instead of waiting on UI that will never appear.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
